  subgraph env["One uv-managed venv — one Python, ordinary Python package deps only;\nthe same on both floors: Linux + NVIDIA and Apple Silicon"]
    app["Stream\n(stream.py: @stream functions over a Stream builder compile the stream's graph\nfrom @node classes — today's app; hosts no node; may expose ports private or public; one venv installs the\npure-Python stream package; the graph is data — one shape with what the\nruntime renders live — that a runtime runs) — built in the streamlib wheel (#2567);\nthe pure-Python stream package is decided, not yet built"]
    procs["Node classes\n(importable modules — imported by the stream,\nregistering their descriptor as the decorator runs, run by processor interpreters;\nnever hosted in the stream's process or the runtime process;\nthe class's import path is its identity)"]
    pkgs["Extension wheels\n(ordinary PyPI packages — Rust inside for speed, a Python processor\nas the binding; depend on the streamlib wheel as a binary, never link the engine;\nnative internals expose handles, never streamlib internals;\ntwo mechanisms — a processor extension added by stream.add that calls its own\nRust directly, and a capability extension: support code declared by a pyproject\nentry point pip records, run once at startup like a driver, sandboxed, able to\nintroduce engine-grade capabilities the engine does not provide; first-party optional capabilities ship this way too,\nnetworking shipped first — streamlib-webrtc (WhipPublisher / WhepPlayer) and\nstreamlib-moq (MoqBroadcastPublisher / MoqBroadcastSubscriber), both on the encoded\nside of the codec blocks, touching no surface and no GPU;\nthe MoQ pair also carries data tracks under streamlib_bag — any bag as a track\nbeside video and audio, named by track_names, the producer's stamp intact,\na late media bag shed and its backlogged group abandoned on the vendored moq-transport;\ngraph carries what loaded as its extensions key;\nlive in packages/, local-linked in-repo,\npublished via the wheel's multi-project index;\ndecided, not yet built: streamlib-webrtc renamed tatolab-webrtc, importing as\ntatolab.webrtc and depending on tatolab-stream; the capability-extension\nhook deleted — no package extends the engine, each sets itself up where its nodes run;\ndecided 2026-10-04: streamlib-moq and its vendored moq-transport are deleted with Zenoh —\nMoQ becomes the engine's own transport off the machine — and streamlib-webrtc stays)"]
    wheel["streamlib wheel\n(Python API + CLI + engine, PyO3 — repo releases now, PyPI after rename;\nbecomes two distributions under a tatolab.* namespace (decided): the pure-Python\ntatolab-stream (tatolab.stream) every stream venv installs and compiles with, no runtime\npresent; and the native tatolab.runtime shipped only with the runtime, lent to each\nprocessor interpreter on PYTHONPATH — a venv holds no engine, and the runtime refuses\nby name what it does not understand in a graph — with no streamlib-owned service\n(decided, not yet built);\none version number for everything released from this repository — tatolab-stream,\nthe runtime and the first-party extensions, released together — and no public Python\nname saying processor (decided, not yet built);\none manylinux wheel and one aarch64-apple-darwin wheel — the macOS one\ncarrying the Vulkan loader and MoltenVK, named to the loader additively;\none _engine.pyi gated by stubtest against both binaries, so the two floors\nare one surface and an absent capability is a closed list refused by name;\nits bag codec is exported as the one encode/decode pair\nan extension carrying a bag over its own transport reaches)"]
    helper["Processor interpreters — every Python node\n(engine exec of sys.executable; own\ninterpreter, own GIL; imports the wheel —\nand refuses to start unless that wheel is the\nparent's own engine build, id checked before\nany channel or socket opens;\nthe only placement;\ndecided, not yet built: exec'd from the stream's own venv interpreter with the\nruntime's lend directory (holding tatolab/runtime/) prepended to PYTHONPATH, so the child\nimports the lent tatolab.runtime beside the venv's tatolab.stream — a venv holds no engine)"]
  end

  rustapp["Rust app\n(plain cargo project)"]
