  engine["Engine runtime\n(runtime/streamlib-engine;\none runtime per machine runs many streams (decided, not yet built):\ntatolabd, owned by one user — another user's runtime is refused; one GpuContext and local API per machine — and, decided 2026-10-04, the machine's MoQ endpoint,\nwith no Zenoh session and no bundled relay; event topic, registry, interpreter,\nlogs, shutdown and interpreter table per stream; streams link freely on the machine;\nrun / run -d (kept, re-loaded on start) / stop / streams / dev; on Apple, an\nSMAppService agent inside Tatolab.app)"]
  media["Built-in media blocks\n(camera / display / MicrophoneSource / SpeakerSink — native,\nin the wheel, handle-shaped primitives;\ncapture on one video device seam — V4L2 on Linux, AVFoundation on Apple —\neach frame carrying its capture instant on both stamps, a future stamp clamped and counted;\nthe Apple event pump on the process's first thread, present from a CAMetalLayer;\naudio backend per platform — CoreAudio AUHAL → null on Apple; on Linux dlopen'd: PipeWire → ALSA → null,\nchosen by opening not by loading; vendored SPA headers\ncompile to a shim that calls only pointers, so no audio\nlibrary enters DT_NEEDED;\ndevice-paced, conditioning on the built-ins;\ncodec blocks: H264/H265 encode+decode on one video codec backend seam —\nVulkan Video on Linux, VideoToolbox on Apple, one Annex-B wire on both —\none encode body and one decode body specialised by codec identity,\ncolour conversion on the engine's existing rgb_to_nv12 — no new RHI primitive;\nall four reach Python as marker classes like every other built-in, and the\nencoded frame has a Python cast (EncodedVideoFrame) holding no surface;\nOpus encode+decode shipped over statically linked libopus, and a pure-Rust\nfragmented Mp4Sink muxing both on every platform — one track per inbound link, named by its channel;\nJpegDecoder retired unbuilt — JPEG decode lives only in Linux MJPEG capture (decided, unbuilt) — and the next codec\nfollows the built-in criterion rather than joining this node — an encoded frame is an\nordinary bag, bitstream inline as bin beside the ordering pair and sync-point flag;\nan encoded audio packet is that convention applied to audio, cast by EncodedAudioPacket;\na decoder publishes the SPS display window, never the padded coded picture;\nVirtualCameraSink (Linux only; no Apple port — a Camera Extension needs a bundle): one camera per processor, created at setup and removed at teardown,\nthat any other application on the machine opens — built-in under criterion (c),\ntwo doors chosen at setup and logged: a v4l2loopback device it creates through the\nmodule's control node, YUYV written by one GPU pass through the RHI's host-pointer\nimport (cached-staging copy where the driver refuses it, imported on the rig), else a\nPipeWire Video/Source node with media.role = Camera over the same dlsym'd shim, whose\nvideo half shares the audio half's entry-point list; the loopback permission is a\none-time enable-virtual-camera the user runs, never elevated by the engine;\ndecided, not yet built: a built-in's type is its class's import path in tatolab.stream\n(tatolab.stream:CameraSource), never its Rust path)"]
  rhi["RHI\n(accelerators optional — a stream that needs no GPU runs on a machine\nwithout one (decided, not yet built);\nvulkan/rhi + streamlib-consumer-rhi —\nthe one Vulkan RHI on both floors, MoltenVK the macOS driver;\nMetal only as handles exported from Vulkan objects;\na driver's missing capability is an absent tier refused by name)"]
  interop["Interop adapters\n(app-process Rust, per floor — Vulkan, cpu-readback, skia on both;\nVulkan↔GL and Vulkan↔CUDA on Linux, named absent on macOS)"]
  ctl["Control plane\n(api-server: HTTP / WS / MCP — engine-side;\nserves the processor catalog — every registered type with its derived\nconfig schema and ports — the live graph, and recipes over its tools;\ndecided, not yet built: one local API per machine, served by the runtime on a socket\nonly the owning user can open — no network address serves control, and another\nmachine's streams are changed on that machine (ssh) or by the control client;\nMCP hosts launch the CLI's mcp verb, a stdio forwarder to the socket (ssh for another\nmachine), and the runtime serves only MCP's current stateless revision, 2026-07-28;\nevery exposed port reachable by URL, on a\nseparate read-only listener — private and public ports on loopback, public ports on the\ntailnet through tailscale serve; decided 2026-10-04: HTTP carries only what is not real time,\nand tap and exchange leave the tool set at the sharing step;\ndecided, not yet built: the tools, the node catalog and the prompts speak the graph's\nwords — add_node / remove_node, connect by node name and port, and none says processor)"]
  cli["CLI — today in the wheel\nnew / dev / run · nodes / graph / tap / logs / exchange · enable-virtual-camera\n(decided 2026-10-04: tap and exchange are deleted at the sharing step;\nnew scaffolds a GlslPixelEffect plus a numpy meter; dev / run print the\ncross-floor check's warnings and never block a start;\ndecided, not yet built: the native tatolab beside tatolabd, shipped with the runtime\nby the installer and never on pip — run / run -d / stop / streams / dev, and the mcp verb)"]
  wire["Wire\n(self-describing bags between nodes —\nthe only cross-language boundary)"]

  registry["Node registry\n(one JSON per live node, inside the one engine-resolved runtime\ndirectory — on Linux XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/streamlib where that is set and non-empty,\notherwise, and on macOS always, /tmp/streamlib-<uid>, owner-only and checked\nbefore the first write — which also holds the\nsurface socket and the engine-owned iceoryx2 domain)"]
  sharing["Sharing off the machine — MoQ on the tailnet (decided 2026-10-04, not yet built):\nTatolab is a simple SDK for defining live streams as pipes and sharing them with people and agents;\nTailscale users first, and nothing Tailscale already does is built — reach, machine names,\nencryption, identity and discovery come from the tailnet; robotics is out of scope;\non one machine streams share data through shared memory; off it, real-time data travels over\nMoQ on QUIC and nothing else — the engine serves a MoQ endpoint itself on its tailnet address,\non the moq-dev line (moq-net, moq-tokio) at exact pins, and a reader subscribes to it directly;\nwith no tailnet a machine shares only with itself and through a relay — nothing is built for a plain LAN;\na machine's name is its tailnet name, read with the list of machines from Tailscale's status;\nwho reads a public port on the tailnet is Tailscale's access rules — no stream map, no peer authentication;\nthe internet edge is a relay the machine has joined, a machine setting: every public port is offered\nthere and sent only while someone subscribes; the runtime joins any relay from an address and a\ncredential, and no relay is written or bundled;\nHTTP carries only what is not real time — the listing, a read-only MCP, snapshots, small samples and\nthe viewer page — on loopback and on the tailnet through tailscale serve, which tatolabd sets up on a\nport of its own when a port first goes public, saying the one command where Tailscale refuses;\nthe viewer page ships with the first version, on the stack's own player — QUIC only, no TCP fallback;\nexposure is internal, private or public, a live map checked at the stream's edge, and a link between\nstreams is always pulled by its reader; the sharing step's details are OPEN.\nShipped today and removed first, by one change: the Zenoh runtime mesh — session, mesh name, discovery,\nremote links, the surface copy across machines, hop-loss counts, mesh peers in graph —\nthe MoQ extension wheel with its vendored moq-transport;\ntap and exchange stay until the sharing step builds the snapshot the rigs read instead;\nuntil the sharing step nothing links one machine to another"]

  ctlclient["External control client\n(decided, not yet built: an extension point —\nstreamlib runs complete without one; how it plugs in is OPEN —\ndirection: an entry point with a role of its own, or another seam;\nsince 2026-10-04 it pushes no stream map — what it hands the runtime beyond a\nrelay address and a credential is OPEN)"]
